  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Calcutta Municipal Corporation vs Shri Kashi Nath Sadhu & Anr on 2 May, 2017",
    "facts": "The prosecution case against the opposite party was to the effect that on 11.7.1983 at about 2.30 P.M., P.W.3 (Food Inspector), D. L. Chatterjee inspected the grocery shop of opposite party no.1 at 1B, Madan Mohan Burman Street, Calcutta and found that opposite party no.2 was selling pepper in the said shop. P.W.3 suspected the pepper to be substandard and collected sample from opposite party no.2, Ashok Kumar Sadhu and sent it for examination by public analyst. It has been alleged that the public analyst was of the opinion that the sample contained mineral oil and was adulterated. Under such circumstances, petition of complaint was filed by P.W.3 after obtaining consent of the Local Health Officer, Dr. S. K. Chowdhury. Prosecution examined four witnesses including P.W.3 (Food Inspector) and Assistant to Local Health Officer (P.W.2). Numbers of documents were also exhibited.",
    "arguments": "Mr. Sanyal, learned senior counsel appearing for the appellant submitted that the opinion of the public analyst (Exhibit 11) shows that there was presence of mineral oil and, accordingly, the order of acquittal ought to be [LEAKAGE_MASK]. In 1996(1) CLJ 10 (Lalit Kishore Gupta Vs State of WB & Ors.) the Court held that in the absence of quantity or percentage of mineral oil being indicated in the report it cannot be said that the sample was adulterated.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Mr. Sanyal, learned senior counsel appearing for the appellant submitted that the opinion of the public analyst (Exhibit 11) shows that there was presence of mineral oil and, accordingly, the order of acquittal ought to be [LEAKAGE_MASK].",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "In 1996(1) CLJ 10 (Lalit Kishore Gupta Vs State of WB & Ors.) the Court held that in the absence of quantity or percentage of mineral oil being indicated in the report it cannot be said that the sample was adulterated."
  },
